                <pb facs="0586" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10901/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Russian Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Russian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In continuation of my
                    note of yesterday, I have the honor to request the provisional detention of Jan
                    Janov Pouren, alias W. Kohks, alias Martin Martinson, living at New York and
                    charged with murder, “robbery” and attempted murders. To that end, I have the
                    honor to have recourse to your excellency’s kindness and to ask that you will
                    kindly send me the certificate, provided by Article VII of the Russo-American
                    extradition treaty, testifying that a request for the extradition of the above
                    named person had been addressed to the Federal Government by the Imperial
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rosen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
